      {
        "id": 76967,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-14T22:47:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The problem of timing and static effects is particularly nasty with Superhuman and Fortitude, because the damage isn't affected by Legacy's reduction until it is being dealt to him, then both would suddenly apply.</p><p>At that point it seems like the reduction would both apply at the same time, which is where card order could come into play.</p><p>I really dislike that entire notion though. &nbsp;Largely because of implications with Tempest's shielding winds. &nbsp;Keeping track of card play order across a table with four or five players is not an enjoyable task, and crosses into too much bookkeeping territory.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:57:47.591Z",
