      {
        "id": 76968,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-14T23:20:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a problem with Stealth and Shielding Winds lately, and never was able to find a certain answer, though in that case at least it was easy enough to figure out card order.&nbsp; One advantage to a computerized version of SOTM would be the ability to timestamp every card in play order, making for easy codification of the rules (which almost read like a programming language already).&nbsp; Assuming of course that &gt;G ever sees any advantage in making a computer-playable version.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
